    "body": "JT2 complete task publication and persistent line Driver handoff — publication notice only, NOT a CLAIM, Driver activation, review, or theorem acceptance.\n\nUser requested all known follow-ups, including the line Driver task, before ending the originating conversation. Atomic main commit: 5ae463f5bb8dd490ef9d7e4b0bfb151ef3f27b15. All five taskbooks and their immutable records were read back at this commit; pinned blobs match. Original generation-1 files remain unchanged.\n\nStart here: https://github.com/awdawmip/enterprise-math/blob/5ae463f5bb8dd490ef9d7e4b0bfb151ef3f27b15/research_notes/EMW59A_JT2_COMPLETE_RELEASE_AND_DRIVER_HANDOFF_20260909.md\n\nParent objective: EM-FREE-W59A-JT2-RAMANUJAN-LEGENDRE (not the unrelated issue-1159 Wallis/sine line).\n\nREADY:\n- GV-EMW59A-JT2-PERSISTENT-LINE-DRIVER — TP2-80471D3D94AE75EFD0AC (GOVERNANCE; requires actual explicit Driver activation).\n- RS-EMW59A-JT2-UR-SUN-PARITY-DEFECT — TP2-22F5729C777040ECA121 (generation 2; same mathematical body).\n- RS-EMW59A-JT2-QTF3-FIXED-POINT — TP2-C2C9DDEB2D65387D115E (generation 2; same mathematical body).\n\nPUBLISHED / BLOCKED with complete machine hard-block fields:\n- RS-EMW59A-JT2-INDEPENDENT-CERTIFICATE-AUDIT — TP2-E9598E6BD0C25FB031D8; needs both exact proof returns and independent verifier.\n- RS-EMW59A-JT2-FINAL-INTEGRATION — TP2-F786E9B728C556CCCCF0; needs accepted compatible certificates, positive independent audit, and original JT2/CM0/transversality/reduction source pins.\n\nThe line Driver owns source recovery, bounded dispatch, exact Result review, follow-up decisions, independent verification, justified formalization and final closure. Recover and consume prior completed proofs; do not restart CM0/transversality merely because chat context is absent. Exact original proof files and the complete JT2 source statement were not pinned in the recovered summaries; keep that source gap explicit. No mathematical proof or active worker is asserted by publication. Source dossier includes all current publication IDs, immutable predecessor refs, precision/valuation/jet/port boundaries, and a reproducible publication checker.",
